  "cwe": [
   {
    "value": "CWE-863",
    "origin": "cna",
    "description": "CWE-863 Incorrect Authorization"
   }
  ],
  "desc": "Improper Authorization vulnerability in Apache ZooKeeper.\n\nWhen SASL authentication is enabled on the client port, the server's SASL callback handler grants every authorization identity (authzid) that a client requests, without checking it against the principal the client authenticated as. The server then tries to replace the requested identity with a canonical form of the authenticated principal, derived from the zookeeper.security.auth_to_local rules. If no rule applies to the principal, canonicalization fails and the error is only logged. The client-requested authzid then becomes the session's SASL identity for all ACL checks.\n\nAn authenticated client whose principal is not covered by the auth_to_local rules can therefore claim any SASL identity. With the default rules, this includes any Kerberos principal from a realm other than the server's default realm, such as a principal from a cross-realm trusted realm. The client then gets the permissions granted to that identity in sasl ACLs. If the requested identity matches a configured zookeeper.superUser, it gets superuser access to the whole data tree.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 3.8.8 or 3.9.7, which fixes the issue.",
  "ranges": [
   {
    "product": "Apache ZooKeeper",
    "min": "3.9.0",
