\n\n \n \n \n Fail-closed SSL verification, HttpClient reuse, and robustness fixes - # 78 # 78 Merged henryx merged 34 commits into jopenlibs:master jopenlibs/vault-java-driver:master from henryx:master henryx/vault-java-driver:master Copy head branch name to clipboard Oct 14, 2026 Conversation Commits 34  ( 34 ) Checks Files changed Merged Fail-closed SSL verification, HttpClient reuse, and robustness fixes # 78 henryx merged 34 commits into jopenlibs:master jopenlibs/vault-java-driver:master from henryx:master henryx/vault-java-driver:master Copy head branch name to clipboard Conversation \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n henryx \n \n\n \n\n \n\n commented\n\n\n Oct 8, 2026 \n\n\n\n \n • \n\n \n \n \n \n edited\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Loading \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n Uh oh!\n \n There was an error while loading. Please reload this page . \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n Copy link\n\n \n \n \n \n Copy Markdown\n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n Collaborator \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n Summary \n This PR mainly fixes SslConfig states that silently disabled SSL certificate verification. It also \nreuses one HTTP client per VaultConfig , makes environment-variable handling stricter, and fixes \nseveral smaller bugs. This PR fixes CVE-2026-109408 \n Security: SSL verification now fails closed \n Before this change, SslConfig.isVerify() could return false when the caller hadn't asked for \nthat. Rest then used a context that trusts every certificate, so chain and hostname checks were \nboth skipped with no error or log. This affected every release that has SslConfig (3.0.0 to \n6.2.3). \n \n \n \n Case \n Before \n After \n \n \n \n \n SslConfig passed to VaultConfig without calling build() \n verification off, pinned cert ignored \n VaultConfig.build() builds it; verification on \n \n \n SslConfig restored by Java deserialization \n no fields restored; verification off \n fields restored ( defaultReadObject() ); verification on unless verify(false) was set \n \n \n VAULT_SSL_VERIFY=1 , t , yes , on or a typo \n verification off \n verification on; unknown values log a warning \n \n \n \n Details: \n \n verify defaults to true , and an explicit verify(Boolean) takes priority even when build() \nhasn't run. \n readObject keeps verification on for data saved by older releases or by never-built instances, \nsince that data can carry a false nobody asked for. \n EnvironmentLoader declares the serialVersionUID that 6.2.3 data carries, so configs \nserialized by 6.2.3 still deserialize. \n The explicit opt-outs, verify(false) and VAULT_SSL_VERIFY=false , still work, with or without \n build() . \n \n Other changes \n \n HTTP client reuse: each VaultConfig keeps one HttpClient and rebuilds it when the SSL \nsettings or timeout change. getHttpClient() returns the client in use instead of null . A \nconfig with a custom client can be serialized; the client itself is not. \n Environment variables: surrounding whitespace is removed and blank values count as unset. \n VAULT_TOKEN and .vault-token are not read when a token is set in code. \n Timeouts: 0 means no timeout again, as before 6.0.0. Negative values are rejected by \n build() ; negative values from environment variables are ignored with a warning. \n Retries: only transient errors are retried (I/O errors and HTTP 5xx, 408, 412, 429). An \ninterrupt stops retrying. \n REST: query parameters are URL-encoded once instead of twice. Response bodies are returned \nbyte-for-byte, so binary content is no longer corrupted. \n Null handling: the response classes tolerate missing or null JSON fields. \n VaultConfig.address(null) falls back to VAULT_ADDR . Vault.create(config, null) throws \n IllegalArgumentException . When no KV engine version is set, version 2 is used. \n Logging: warnings go to java.util.logging instead of stderr. \n Deprecations: methods documented as deprecated now also carry @Deprecated , so callers get \na compiler warning: Vault.leases() , mounts() and seal() (and their VaultImpl \noverrides), plus Auth.lookupWrap() , unwrap() , wrap() and rewrap() . Use the Sys \nequivalents, e.g. vault.sys().leases() and vault.sys().wrapping() . Auth.loginByAppID() \ngains a @deprecated Javadoc tag pointing to loginByAppRole() . \n Javadoc examples: Leases , Mounts and Wrapping examples use the sys() calls instead \nof the deprecated ones. The Wrapping examples also used new Vault(config) (an interface) and \na misspelled lookupWarp() , and one referred to an undefined variable; all are fixed. \n Build/CI: Maven plugin versions are pinned, Checkstyle runs and fails the build on \nviolations, CI test reports are fixed, and the Travis config is removed. The CI matrix drops \nVault 1.8.12–1.15.6 and adds 2.1.0–2.1.2, so it now tests Vault 1.16.3 to 2.1.2 and latest . \n \n Breaking or behaviour changes \n \n VAULT_SSL_VERIFY=0 , no or off now keep verification on . Use false to disable it. \n 4xx responses other than 408, 412 and 429 now fail immediately instead of being retried . \n Logical.getEngineVersionForSecretPath() returns 2 instead of null when no version is set. \n VaultConfig.nameSpace() no longer throws; an empty namespace is rejected by build() . \n getSecretsEnginePathMap() returns an unmodifiable map. \n A config serialized by 6.2.3 that was built with VAULT_SSL_VERIFY=false comes back with \nverification on. \n Vault 1.8 to 1.15 are deprecated: they are no longer tested in CI. Code that only applies to \nthem (the App ID integration test and its setup, and the pre-1.13 PKI status-code branches) is \nmarked as deprecated. \n Calls to the methods newly annotated @Deprecated now produce compiler warnings. \n \n Known limitations (documented in the README) \n \n A JKS keystore or truststore isn't serialized. A restored JKS-based SslConfig checks the server \nagainst the JVM's default CAs, so it still verifies but loses the pinned CA. \n Certificate settings changed after build() only apply once build() is called again. \n \n Tests \n \n New SslConfigSerializationTests : round-trips of SslConfig and VaultConfig , data saved by \nnever-built instances, and fixtures written by release 6.2.3 \n( src/test/resources/serialized-6.2.3/ ). \n New tests in VaultConfigTests (environment variables, VAULT_SSL_VERIFY parsing, timeouts) \nplus tests for retries, response bodies and null handling. \n \n Thanks \n Special thanks to Echo to help to find this problem \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n --> \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Sorry, something went wrong.\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n Uh oh!\n \n There was an error while loading. Please reload this page . \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n --> \n \n \n \n \n \n All reactions \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n henryx \n \n\n added 30 commits\n October 6, 2026 22:37 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Reused HttpClient object \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n f1bf44c \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Returned response at same mode as returned from remote resource \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n 67566e7 \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Checked if an operation is retryable \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n 068dc20 \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Fixed CI \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n 99002eb \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Removed Travis CI \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n fd9514e \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Pinned versions \n \n\n \n\n \