  "text": " \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n Paper page - On the Generalization Limitation of On-Policy Distillation for Post-RL Consolidation \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n Hugging Face Models Datasets Spaces Buckets Docs Enterprise Pricing Website Tasks HuggingChat Collections Languages Organizations Community Blog Posts Daily Papers Hardware Learn Discord Forum GitHub Solutions Team & Enterprise Hugging Face PRO Enterprise Support Inference Providers Inference Endpoints Storage Buckets Log In Sign Up Hi everyone! I’m the first author of this paper.</p>\\n<p>We identify a blind spot in (M)OPD for post-RL consolidation: students may not inherit their teachers’ generalization capabilities, even when they achieve near-perfect in-distribution distillation performance.</p>\\n<p>We investigate this on a large scale, across math, coding, agent, and long-context tasks, using different student and teacher models.</p>\\n<p>We also analyze and explore preliminary patching methods. We’d love to discuss more about how to further improve generalization in (M)OPD!</p>\\n<p>Project page: <a href=\\\"https://yichenzw.com/opd-generalization.github.io/\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">https://yichenzw.com/opd-generalization.github.io/</a></p>\\n<p>Huge thanks to all my co-authors for their contributions to this project!</p>\\n\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-11-05T06:25:17.205Z\",\"author\":{\"_id\":\"6484fe4e22e3c63f5ec0a23a\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6484fe4e22e3c63f5ec0a23a/roXzheKehiq2m60b_gXwX.png\",\"fullname\":\"Yichen Zach Wang\",\"name\":\"ZachW\",\"type\":\"user\",\"isPro\":false,\"isHf\":false,\"isHfAdmin\":false,\"isMod\":false,\"followerCount\":3,\"isUserFollowing\":false}},\"numEdits\":1,\"identifiedLanguage\":{\"language\":\"en\",\"probability\":0.9064429402351379},\"editors\":[\"ZachW\"],\"editorAvatarUrls\":[\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6484fe4e22e3c63f5ec0a23a/roXzheKehiq2m60b_gXwX.png\"],\"reactions\":[],\"isReport\":false}},{\"id\":\"6aec478a0ac465e3f0f082d9\",\"author\":{\"_id\":\"6ad5468b4aeb52627d66244e\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/noauth/CplAfKR5c4jxPAKNSXJw4.jpeg\",\"fullname\":\"Victor Grösser\",\"name\":\"orinmemory\",\"type\":\"user\",\"isPro\":false,\"isHf\":false,\"isHfAdmin\":false,\"isMod\":false,\"isUserFollowing\":false},\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-05T09:08:26.000Z\",\"type\":\"comment\",\"data\":{\"edited\":false,\"hidden\":false,\"latest\":{\"raw\":\"Great to see OOD retention measured separately from IND distillation quality; \\\"near-perfect IND can mask incomplete consolidation\\\" is something many people assume but rarely quantify. For me the most practical result is base-preserving replay: adding coding prompts supervised by the base model lifts AIME25 avg@8 to 67.50 for the GSM8K OPD student, with only a 0.18-point drop on GSM8K. Did you look at how the replay ratio trades off against IND performance, and whether replay and Procrustes-attention patching stack?\",\"html\":\"<p>Great to see OOD retention measured separately from IND distillation quality; \\\"near-perfect IND can mask incomplete consolidation\\\" is something many people assume but rarely quantify. For me the most practical result is base-preserving replay: adding coding prompts supervised by the base model lifts AIME25 avg@8 to 67.50 for the GSM8K OPD student, with only a 0.18-point drop on GSM8K. Did you look at how the replay ratio trades off against IND performance, and whether replay and Procrustes-attention patching stack?</p>\\n\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-11-05T09:08:26.633Z\",\"author\":{\"_id\":\"6ad5468b4aeb52627d66244e\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/noauth/CplAfKR5c4jxPAKNSXJw4.jpeg\",\"fullname\":\"Victor Grösser\",\"name\":\"orinmemory\",\"type\":\"user\",\"isPro\":false,\"isHf\":false,\"isHfAdmin\":false,\"