engineering experience led you to believe the magic of multiple decades guaranteeing improvements? reply hendrikmans 3 hours ago | root | parent | next [–] \n Are you claiming that browsers, their renderers, V8 etc. are slow and unoptimized? reply anthk 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] \n > a11y, IME, RTL Artcraft it's doing that in every software application; > so you add a scripting layer, maybe integrate a little Lua VM or something that lets you execute JavaScript? Every Arftcraft software can be command line driven and it's still fast and small compared to your bloated crap. reply elevaet 5 hours ago | prev | next [–] \n Hopefully we will get an Electron-free VSCode too at some point. edit: there is one https://github.com/Sidenai/sidex haven't tried it yet reply teekert 1 hour ago | parent | next [–] \n You mean Zed? https://zed.dev/ reply eastbound 6 hours ago | prev [–] \n That's a direct benefit from AI. If all products ditch Electron, it satisfies the NSA requirements of having AI-generated backdoors on your computer, while allowing you to reduce your RAM consumption and letting this precious silicon for Sam Altman (He's quoted saying RAM is better spent in data centers than in personal computers - and in an era where everything is Cloud, one might wonder why the base Macbook Pro has 32GB). reply \n \n Guidelines | FAQ | Lists | API | Security | Legal | Apply to YC | Contact \n Search: "
