  "text": " The Stacks Project, Formalized in Lean | Hacker News Hacker News new | past | comments | ask | show | jobs | submit login The Stacks Project, Formalized in Lean ( axiommath.ai ) 43 points by namanbnsl 3 hours ago | hide | past | favorite | 8 comments help \n \n QuesnayJr 2 hours ago | next [–] \n After they announced the formalization of the classification of Finite Simple Groups, I immediately wondered \"What would happen if you tried to formalize the Stacks Project?\" Despite also being very long, it's the opposite of the CFSG: instead of a poorly organized set of results that contribute to proving one big theorem, it's instead a carefully-organized set of results that cover a broad area. The Stacks Project was the model for how mathematics should be done (at least for the pre-LLM era). Algebraic geometry had lots of poorly organized foundational results that were not really created for themselves, but in order to solve problems in the field. One person, Aise Johan de Jong, set out to fix it by organizing a project to write out the proofs of all of the results in a carefully organized fashion. He's led the project since, though of course there are multiple contributors. The whole thing is thousands of pages. I would be interested in hearing more about the gaps they uncovered in the existing results, and how they fixed them. reply AlexCoventry 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] \n Do they say how they verified the formalizations of the theorem hypotheses? (Sorry, I haven't read it yet.) reply vatsachak 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] \n Okay this is actually useful AI formalization. But the stacks project is basically Lean in natural language anyways, so it makes sense why its high quality. reply eternauta3k 2 hours ago | prev | next [–] \n Slightly off-topic, but how far are we from a formally verified stack for (say) a webdav or NFS server? reply breezybottom 2 hours ago | prev [–] \n The fact that the description is AI slop doesn't inspire confidence in the results. reply viccis 2 hours ago | parent | next [–] \n Slop Verbiage, Straight To Your HN Feed reply browningstreet 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] \n Axiom raises $264M, publishes this massive lean proof built with AI, and you're moaning about some AI language in their description. AI is in their domain name. What are you doing? reply joe_the_user 1 hour ago | parent | prev [–] \n Yes, \"This milestone begins with the Stacks Project itself\". Could half AI slop effects be mitigated by a prompt \"Don't mix or mangle metaphors here\"? A milestone is a step in a process, not the entire process. Once this kind of sloppy effort to sound impressive was just \"over writing\" but its now a strong tell for AI. reply \n \n Guidelines | FAQ | Lists | API | Security | Legal | Apply to YC | Contact \n Search: "
 },
