  "text": "\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n GitHub - rivet-dev/rivet: The orchestrator for agentic workloads. A fast, high-density and scalable orchestrator for every workload an agent needs. · GitHub \n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n Skip to content \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n Navigation Menu Sign in Products Platform GitHub Repository hosting, code review, and collaboration Copilot AI coding agent for tasks, projects, and automated work Build & Ship Actions CI/CD and automation Code Quality Quality analysis, fixes, and enforcement Codespaces Cloud development environments Secure Code Security Vulnerability detection and remediation Secret Protection Secret scanning and leak prevention All Features Developers Learn Documentation Training Certifications Build Build with Copilot Customize Copilot Integrations Explore Trending repos GitHub Sponsors Developer articles Changelog Changelog Your source for the latest features, improvements, and fixes across GitHub products, all in one place. Businesses By Stage Enterprises Team Startups Nonprofits By Industry Healthcare Financial services Manufacturing Government See all industries Evaluate GitHub Why GitHub Customer Stories Business insights Trust Center Add-ons GitHub Advanced Security Enterprise-grade code security Copilot for business Enterprise-grade AI features Premium Support Enterprise-grade 24/7 support Resources Learn & Connect Documentation Resource center Blog Events & webinars Community Forum Customer Stories Integrations Support Customer support Training GitHub Status Company About Partners Changelog GitHub Universe GitHub Universe The event for developers, by developers — talks, workshops, and what’s next for GitHub. Pricing Search / Sign in Sign up Appearance settings \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. \n You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. \n You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. \n\n \n Dismiss alert \n\n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n {{ message }} \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n rivet-dev rivet Repository navigation Code Issues 46  ( 46 ) Pull requests 334  ( 334 ) Discussions Actions Security and quality Insights More items \n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n rivet Public Notifications You must be signed in to change notification settings Fork 306  ( 306 ) Star 6.6k  ( 6.6k ) You must be signed in to star a repository About The orchestrator for agentic workloads. A fast, high-density and scalable orchestrator for every workload an agent needs. www.rivet.dev Topics actor actors cloudflare cloudflare-durable-objects durable-objects foundationdb multiplayer realtime rust serverless Resources Readme Apache-2.0 license Activity Custom properties Stars 6.6k stars Watchers 19 watching Forks 306 forks Report repository main Branches Tags Go to file Code Open more actions menu Latest commit   History 6,316 Commits 6,316 Commits Folders and files Name Name Last commit message Last commit date .cargo .cargo     .github .github     docker docker     docs docs     engine engine     examples examples     integrations integrations     rivetkit-asyncapi rivetkit-asyncapi     rivetkit-json-schema rivetkit-json-schema     rivetkit-openapi rivetkit-openapi     rivetkit-python/ client rivetkit-python/ client     rivetkit-rust rivetkit-rust     rivetkit-swift rivetkit-swift     rivetkit-typescript rivetkit-typescript     scripts scripts     shared/ typescript shared/ typescript     vendor vendor     .dockerignore .dockerignore     .editorconfig .editorconfig     .gitattributes .gitattributes     .gitignore .gitignore     CHANGELOG.md CHANGELOG.md     Cargo.lock Cargo.lock     Cargo.toml Cargo.toml     LICENSE LICENSE     README.md README.md     biome.json biome.json     clippy.toml clippy.toml     deny.toml deny.toml     justfile justfile     package.json package.json     pnpm-lock.yaml pnpm-lock.yaml     pnpm-workspace.yaml pnpm-workspace.yaml     rust-toolchain.toml rust-toolchain.toml     rustfmt.toml rustfmt.toml     tsconfig.base.json tsconfig.base.json     tsup.base.ts tsup.base.ts     turbo.json turbo.json     View all files Repository files navigation README Apache-2.0 license More items \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Fast, high-density, scalable orchestration with Rivet Actors. Built on S3 at SSD speeds. \n \n 4.99 ms p99 cold starts, 72 KB RAM per Actor, scales to billions\n \n \n Quickstart •\n Documentation •\n Changelog •\n Discord •\n X \n \n \n What is Rivet? \n Rivet is an orchestrator for agentic workloads built on the actor model. Each Rivet Actor is a long-lived process with in-memory state, a SQLite database, WebSockets for realtime, and scheduling, addressed by key. Create one per agent, session, user, or tenant, and run it on plain Node.js, Bun, or Rust. \n \n 72 KB per Actor : Actors share a node process instead of each booting a sandbox, so one server holds hundreds of thousands. \n 4.99 ms p99 cold starts : No image pull and no VM boot. \n SQLite backed by S3, at SSD speeds : 1.07 ms durable writes and 1.36 ms reads at p99, for about 10.4× less than replicated SSD storage. \n Hibernates when idle : Idle Actors cost nothing and wake on the next request with nothing lost. \n \n Backend \n import { actor } from \"rivetkit\" ; \n import { db } from \"rivetkit/db\" ; \n\n const agent = actor ( { \n // Per-Actor SQLite database, persisted across restarts and hibernation \n db : db ( { \n onMigrate : async ( db ) => { \n // Apply the SQLite schema \n await db . execute ( `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS messages (role TEXT, content TEXT)` ) ; \n } , \n } ) , \n\n actions : { \n chat : async ( c , text : string ) => { \n // Durably save the message \n await c . db . execute ( \"INSERT INTO messages VALUES (?, ?)\" , \"user\" , text ) ; \n const messages = await c . db . execute ( \"SELECT role, content FROM messages\" ) ; \n\n const response = streamText ( { model : openai ( \"gpt-5\" ) , messages } ) ; \n\n // Stream tokens to every connected client for multiplayer \n for await ( const delta of response . textStream ) { \n c . broadcast ( \"token\" , delta ) ; \n } \n\n // Durably save the response \n await c . db . execute ( \"INSERT INTO messages VALUES (?, ?)\" , \"assistant\" , await response . text ) ; \n } , \n } , \n } ) ; \n Client (frontend or backend) \n // Connect to an Actor \n const agent = client . agent . getOrCreate ( \"agent-123\" ) . connect ( ) ; \n\n // Listen for realtime events \n agent . on ( \"token\" , delta => process . stdout . write ( delta ) ) ; \n\n // Call an action on the Actor \n await agent . chat ( \"how many r's in strawberry?\" ) ; \n Getting Started \n Use with your coding agent \n Paste this prompt into Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, or any coding agent: \n Run npx skills add rivet-dev/skills, then ask me what to build and run it locally.\n \n Start from scratch \n Every product Rivet ships is an Actor, scheduled by the same control plane. \n \n Actors : Long-lived processes with state, realtime, and scheduling built in. \n Agents : A durable process per agent, with memory that survives restarts. \n Workflows : Multi-step operations that replay instead of starting over. \n agentOS : Run the code your agent writes, securely, with granular control over network access, filesystem access, and resource limits. \n Dynamic Apps (preview): A backend per user, deployed the moment it is generated. \n \n Built for everything agents need \n \n Coding agents : One Actor per agent, with a durable process and state that survives restarts. \n Agent app builders : Each generated backend deploys as its own Actor that scales to zero. \n Agents in your VPC : Run agents next to your databases and APIs, so no data leaves your cloud. \n Realtime apps : One Actor per document, room, or channel, broadcasting changes to every client. \n \n How Actors compare to sandboxes \n \n \n \n Metric \n Rivet Actor \n Sandbox \n \n \n \n \n Cold start (p99) \n 4.99 ms \n 1.70 s \n \n \n Memory per instance \n 72.4 KB \n 512 MiB \n \n \n Storage \n SQLite on S3 \n Disk per sandbox \n \n \n Storage cost \n 10.4× cheaper \n Replicated SSDs \n \n \n \n \n Benchmark details & methodology \n \n Rivet numbers come from the published Rivet Actors vs Cloudflare Durable Objects benchmark , run on Rivet 3.0.3. Its repository has the raw samples and the scripts to reproduce them. \n Sandbox numbers are a documented default memory allocation and a third-party cold start benchmark. \n Storage cost compares S3 Standard with three Amazon EBS gp3 copies at AWS list prices. \n Sources, dates, and the full method are at rivet.dev/docs/benchmarking . \n \n \n Features \n \n Fault tolerance : If a node goes down, its Actors move elsewhere with their state intact. \n HTTP & WebSocket networking : Call an Actor over HTTP or hold a live WebSocket to it. \n End-to-end type safety : Typed clients for your backend and React hooks for your frontend. \n Cron & scheduling : Wake an Actor on a schedule or at a time it sets for itself. \n Actor-to-Actor calls : Actors call each other by key across the cluster. \n OpenTelemetry : Traces, metrics, and logs in OTel format. \n \n Deployment Options \n \n \n \n Option \n Description \n Get started \n \n \n \n \n Local & self-host \n Run Rivet locally while you build. In production, run the control plane on Docker, Kubernetes, or a VM. S3 is the only dependency. \n Self-hosting docs \n \n \n Rivet Cloud \n Fully managed, dedicated clusters on AWS or GCP in any region. Run your nodes on Rivet Cloud or bring your own. \n Dashboard \n \n \n BYOC \n The control plane runs inside your own VPC on AWS, GCP, or Azure, fully managed by Rivet. Your data never leaves your cloud. \n BYOC docs \n \n \n \n Every option runs the same control plane, from local dev to production. Talk to an engineer → \n Works with the tools you already use \n Typed SDKs for your backend and React hooks for your frontend. Rivet runs on native Node.js and Bun with no custom runtime, so your existing packages, tooling, and tests work unchanged. \n Deploy nodes on : Docker Compose • Kubernetes • VM & bare metal • Hetzner • AWS ECS • Railway • Render \n Frameworks : React • Effect \n Runtimes : Node.js • Bun • Rust \n Tools : Vitest • OpenTelemetry • Pino • AI SDK • OpenAPI • AsyncAPI \n Request an integration → \n FAQ \n \n Does Rivet have BYOC? \n Yes. Rivet deploys into your own cloud account, including air-gapped environments: the control plane and storage run inside your VPC while Rivet operates them. See the BYOC docs . \n \n \n Does Rivet have a cloud? \n Yes. Rivet Cloud runs fully managed, dedicated clusters on AWS or GCP in any region. It can run your app's Docker image as nodes on Rivet Cloud , or you can bring your own nodes . \n \n \n Can I self-host Rivet? \n Yes. Rivet is fully self-hostable; see the self-hosting docs . The control plane runs anywhere a container runs, with guides for Docker Compose, Kubernetes, VMs and bare metal, Hetzner, Railway, Render, and AWS ECS. For enterprise support with a self-hosted deployment, contact us . \n \n \n Do I still need Postgres, FoundationDB, or NATS? \n No. An object storage bucket is the only dependency: there is no database to run and no message bus, and control plane instances find each other through the bucket. Rivet works with Amazon S3, Google Cloud Storage, Azure Blob Storage, and any S3-compatible store such as MinIO, Cloudflare R2, or Hetzner Object Storage. A local filesystem backend is available for trying Rivet on one machine. \n \n \n Is Rivet open-source? \n Yes. Rivet is open source under the permissive Apache 2.0 license. You're looking at it. \n \n \n How does Rivet compare to sandboxes? \n A sandbox boots a VM or container per agent, which is slow to start and sits mostly idle. A Rivet Actor runs inside a shared node process: 72 KB and 4.99 ms p99 to start, versus 512 MiB and 1.70 s for a sandbox, and it hibernates when idle. To run untrusted code your agent writes, use agentOS . \n \n \n How does Rivet compare to Cloudflare Durable Objects? \n Rivet is often used as an open-source alternative to Cloudflare Durable Objects that is easy to self-host and scales. It also fixes many of the constraints of Durable Objects: no 128 MB memory cap, bottomless storage instead of a 10 GB SQLite limit, Actors are not randomly evicted, and you control the runtime because Actors run on vanilla Node.js or Bun instead of a custom runtime. Rivet also adds built-in connection handling, event broadcasting, durable scheduling and cron, full Vitest support, lifecycle hooks for draining, and control over Actor upgrades. See the Cloudflare Durable Objects comparison . \n \n \n Does Rivet use a custom V8 runtime? \n No. Rivet runs on native Node.js and Bun, so your existing packages, tooling, and tests work unchanged. \n \n \n Is Rivet like Erlang, Akka, or Orleans? \n Rivet implements the virtual actor pattern, which is closest to Orleans, but focuses on what modern workloads need: SQLite persistence instead of simple JSON stores and support for modern runtimes. Erlang and Akka do not provide virtual actors out of the box, though ecosystem packages exist that offer functionality comparable to Rivet Actors. \n \n \n Does Rivet require microVMs, gVisor, or nested virtualization? \n No. Rivet only needs a standard process that connects to the control plane over WebSocket. That process can be Node.js, Bun, Rust, or anything else. \n \n Projects in This Repository \n \n \n \n Project \n Description \n \n \n \n \n RivetKit TypeScript \n Client & server library for building Actors \n \n \n RivetKit Rust \n Rust SDK \n \n \n RivetKit Python \n Python client (experimental) \n \n \n RivetKit Swift \n Swift client (experimental) \n \n \n Control Plane \n Rust control plane that schedules, routes, and persists Actors \n \n \n ↳ Pegboard \n Actor scheduling & networking \n \n \n ↳ Gasoline \n Durable execution engine \n \n \n ↳ Guard \n Traffic routing proxy \n \n \n ↳ Epoxy \n Multi-region KV store (EPaxos) \n \n \n Dashboard \n Inspector for debugging Actors \n \n \n Documentation \n Source for rivet.dev/actors/docs \n \n \n Examples \n Runnable examples \n \n \n \n Community \n \n Discord - Chat with the community \n X/Twitter - Follow for updates \n Bluesky - Follow for updates \n GitHub Discussions - Ask questions \n GitHub Issues - Report bugs \n Talk to an engineer - Discuss your use case \n \n License \n Apache 2.0 \n About The orchestrator for agentic workloads. A fast, high-density and scalable orchestrator for every workload an agent needs. www.rivet.dev Topics actor actors cloudflare cloudflare-durable-objects durable-objects foundationdb multiplayer realtime rust serverless Resources Readme Apache-2.0 license Activity Custom properties Stars 6.6k stars Watchers 19 watching Forks 306 forks Report repository Releases Used by Contributors Languages \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n \n Footer \n\n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n &copy; 2026 GitHub, Inc.\n \n \n\n \n Footer navigation \n\n \n\n\n \n Terms \n \n\n \n Privacy \n \n\n\n \n Security \n \n\n \n Status \n \n\n \n Community \n \n\n \n Docs \n \n\n \n Contact \n \n\n \n \n \n \n Manage cookies\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n Do not share my personal information\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n You can’t perform that action at this time.\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n"
